# @javadaba/* packages resolve from Javadaba's private registry (GitHub Packages),
# NOT the public npm registry. @javadaba/daba-engine is closed-source (see
# docs/superpowers/backlog/2026-07-17-daba-engine-registro-privado.md and, in the
# javadaba-web Core, docs/adr/0003-daba-engine-cerrado-registro-privado.md): only the
# compiled dist/ + type declarations are published here, never the TypeScript source.
#
# `npm install` needs a read token with the `read:packages` scope exported as
# NODE_AUTH_TOKEN (or NPM_TOKEN) in the environment — see the backlog entry above for
# local-dev alternatives (npm link) while the registry publish (Task 9 Step 3) is
# pending authorization.
@javadaba:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
